Commercial use includes any use intended primarily for financial gain, commercial advantage, or business operations.

## 3. Fork Identification

Any distributed version of the Software that has been modified from the original version must clearly and prominently identify itself as a fork, modified version, or derivative work of the original Software.

The identification must make clear that the modified version is not the official version of the original Software.

Acceptable examples include:

- "Fork of GO Live"
- "Modified version of Go Live"
- "Based on Go Live"
- "Unofficial fork of Go Live"

The identification must not be removed, hidden, or presented in a manner reasonably likely to cause users to believe that the modified version is the official version of the original Software.

